    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>We offer two tiers of support to help you get the most out of our tools.</p>

    <h2>Best Effort Support</h2>
    <p>For community support, please open an issue in the appropriate repository on GitHub. We try to respond to all community inquiries in a timely manner, though response times may vary.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/scan/issues" target="_blank">scan</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/cleave/issues" target="_blank">cleave</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/azoth/issues" target="_blank">azoth</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/atomdrift-project/stng/issues" target="_blank">stng</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Commercial Support, Rule Updates &amp; Hosted API</h2>
    <p>Our corporate sponsor, <a href="https://isotope13.ai/" target="_blank"><strong class="isotope-brand">isotope¹³</strong></a>, offers real-time rule feeds, SLA-backed support, and integration consulting.</p>
    <p>If you would rather not run the scanners yourself, isotope¹³ also offers a <a href="https://isotope13.ai/enriched/" target="_blank">hosted scanning API</a>. Send it a package URL, a SHA-256, or a raw file and get the same verdict, with the same evidence, from the same open-source engine.</p>
